{"toolCallId":"call_ca52675c929847ac99f2dc1a1ad1ef65","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"spec.md:95:| REQ-007 | With `--quiet`, any warning the script writes to stderr is still written to stderr, so `--quiet` trims stdout only. |\ntasks.md:50:- [ ] T014 Leave stderr untouched on the quiet path: the quiet branch prints its one line to stdout with no stderr redirect, so any warning the script emits still reaches stderr (REQ-007) (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n 'QUIET_OUTPUT' $S` shows no `2>` redirect on the quiet branch, and `bash $S --quiet --loc 500 --files 15 2>/dev/null | wc -l` prints `1`.\nacceptance-criteria.md:60:| AC-007 | REQ-007 | Given a run that writes a warning to stderr, When `--quiet` is passed, Then the warning still reaches stderr and stdout holds only the level line | `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --quiet --loc 500 --files 15 2>/dev/null \\| wc -l` prints `1`, and the quiet branch carries no stderr redirect (T014) | Unmet | - |\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w1eb206b128/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"3875c8","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
